<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Not our self-appointed task</l><l>Will the Lord’s approval win,</l><l>But the work we did not ask,</l><l>Finished humbly, just for Him.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Not the prayer we long to plead</l><l>When we bend before the Throne,</l><l>But the touching deeper need</l><l>Of the Spirit’s wordless groan.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Not the gift we proudly lay</l><l>On His altar will He heed,</l><l>If our hearts have said Him, “Nay,”</l><l>When He whispered, “I have need.”</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Thus we die, and dying live</l><l>In the heavenlies with the Lord;</l><l>Thus we serve, and pray, and give,</l><l>Christ Himself our great Reward.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
